  "description": "Marble is a centralized AML and risk decision engine used to evaluate customers, transactions, and wallets.\nInstead of only checking data, Marble runs configured compliance rules and returns a clear decision such as Approve, Review, Block and Review, or Decline, along with the reason and risk score.\nIt also supports sanctions, PEP, and watchlist screening, helping cover AML checks beyond the initial Sumsub KYC verification.\nCompliance teams can manage and update risk rules directly in Marble without requiring code changes or application deployments.\nEvery decision is recorded with a complete audit trail, making it easier for compliance analysts and auditors to understand why a customer or transaction was approved, reviewed, or declined.\nIn our application, Marble is integrated through the IAmlProvider and IAmlProviderFactory pattern. This keeps the implementation provider-independent and allows us to switch between Marble, Sumsub, or None using configuration.\nMarble can be used throughout the customer lifecycle — during customer approval, transaction processing, and wallet risk checks. It also supports ongoing monitoring, allowing customers and other objects to be re-screened when AML rules or sanctions data change.",
